--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bring-up/j72-firmware.md
@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@
+# J72 firmware inputs
+
+The J72 recipe identifies iPad Air Cellular (`iPad4,2`, J72AP) inputs from
+iOS 12.5.7 build 16H81. Firmware and per-device calibration remain private.
+
+The recipe generates only `apple/j72-fwstart.z2fw` through the model-selected
+native N1 converter. Its output is the same 57,256-byte input that passed the
+J72 native RAM touch tests. It contains no unit calibration. A console payload
+can keep its existing `firmware = false` project setting.
+
+This enables standard firmware preparation for future recovery/installation;
+it does not qualify installed startup or enable storage installation. The J72
+descriptor still has installation disabled.
+
+The recipe's complete 2,961,469,678-byte IPSW was downloaded from the stated
+Apple CDN URL and its SHA-256 verified. Its BuildManifest identifies iOS
+12.5.7/16H81 and J72AP with CPID `0x8960`, BDID `0x12`, and product `iPad4,2`.
+
+## Touch input and remaining conversion work
+
+`J72.mtprops` is the decoded logical file, not its empty on-disk data fork.
+Its SHA-256 is
+`69f27fe207cc5810a748dac3dfe640b1c5a755709f49513b4b5125660784f0fc`
+and its logical size is 80,301 bytes. It uses a `com.apple.decmpfs` type-4
+attribute and a `com.apple.ResourceFork` containing zlib blocks. The existing
+Orchard resource-fork decoder reproduces the privately extracted file exactly.
+
+The iOS 12.5.7 system image is APFS. Orchard's existing UDIF reader, APFS volume
+lookup, extended-attribute lookup and type-4 decompression read this path
+without changes, producing bytes equal to the private logical file. This is
+the system image; recovery RAM images are separate inputs and may use another
+filesystem. No HFS+ reader is needed for this firmware recipe.
+
+The normal `Ipsw.system_file()` path was also checked against the Apple CDN:
+it fetched 2,067,491 bytes by range and returned the same 80,301-byte logical
+file. That check covers ZIP member selection, UDIF, APFS and decompression.
+It does not convert the file or qualify touch hardware.
+
+The generated bytes passed native RAM firmware startup, touch interaction and
+normal supply cleanup on this J72. Installed-system automatic startup remains
+unqualified; extraction or package assembly alone does not establish it.
+
+## Native N1 candidate contract
+
+The model-selected `z2fw-from-z2-packet@2` step preserves existing Z2FW
+version-1 framing. The active recipe names `apple/j72-fwstart.z2fw` with these
+parameters:
+
+```json
+{
+  "step": "z2fw-from-z2-packet@2",
+  "input": "J72.mtprops",
+  "profile": "C1F15,1",
+  "calibration_address": 268472320,
+  "calibration_size": 1024,
+  "prox_address": 268473856,
+  "prox_size": 128
+}
+```
+
+The four records, in order, are:
+
+| Record | Content |
+|---|---|
+| CONFIG (4) | Eleven little-endian u32 words: `0x818`, nine zeros, `0x103`; mode 0 and explicit legacy full-word HBPP counts |
+| SEND (1) | A 144-byte legacy blob loading 128 zero proximity bytes at `0x10009600` |
+| CALIBRATION (6) | Three little-endian u32 words: address `0x10009000`, maximum 1024 bytes, provider 0 |
+| SEND (1) | The unchanged 57,016-byte `Constructed Firmware` packet from `C1F15,1` |
+
+The generated candidate is 57,256 bytes, SHA-256
+`73ca290607695ca841867a2bf76cab4bc2f5c33b9ab5ac171de5b5580a7c0c09`.
+The proximity and firmware wire packets match the private working RAM worker
+byte for byte. An independent reconstruction of the dynamic 1008-byte and
+16-byte calibration chunks also matches that worker. These byte comparisons are separate from hardware results. Native RAM tests
+on 4 November confirmed startup, menu/terminal touch and keyboard interaction;
+normal removal returned all three supplies to disabled with zero users. No
+installed-system or storage qualification is claimed.
+
+The native N1 driver owns warm-up, reset, HBPP readiness, register calibration,
+the 65 ms calibration wait, execute and runtime discovery. Those commands must
+not also appear in this firmware file. In particular, `z2fw-from-mtprops@3`
+includes a different driver's INIT and register sequence and is not suitable
+for this native N1 loader.
+
+## Per-device calibration
+
+The firmware output contains no owner's calibration. Provider 0 consumes
+`apple,z2-cal-blob` on the touchscreen node. Existing m1n1 code copies the
+running unit's ADT `multi-touch-calibration` into that property through the
+`touchscreen0` FDT alias. Unresolved `syscfg/` references are not copied.
+
+The native driver must require exactly 1024 bytes, reject absent, all-zero and
+all-`0xff` data before powering the controller, then send it in 1008-byte and
+16-byte chunks. It must not substitute another unit's calibration or an IPSW
+default. The zero proximity packet is a separate, observed model initialization;
+it does not replace this mandatory unit calibration.
+
+Before qualifying an output, test the exact native kernel, providers, device
+tree, m1n1 and privately generated firmware together. Check the calibration
+property's presence and size without publishing its bytes, then verify boot,
+touch events, coordinates, release handling and normal cleanup on the device.
